BT
/Times 22 Tf
1 0 0 1 72 720 Tm
(Waves at the Edge) Tj
/Times 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 72 690 Tm
() Tj
/Times 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 72 672 Tm
(There are two ways to keep an archive of a coast. The first is to photograph it, which) Tj
/Times 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 72 654 Tm
(is a way of saying: this is how it looked, and I was here to see it. The second is to) Tj
/Times 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 72 636 Tm
(measure it, which is a way of admitting that the photograph was already out of date.) Tj
/Times 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 72 618 Tm
() Tj
/Times 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 72 600 Tm
(A tide table is not a description of the sea. It is a promise the moon makes to a) Tj
/Times 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 72 582 Tm
(harbour master, written down in advance so that boats can be loaded and nets mended.) Tj
/Times 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 72 564 Tm
(When the table says low water at 06:12, it means: be there at 06:12, and the sea will) Tj
/Times 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 72 546 Tm
(have done its part. Most of the time, it has. The table's usefulness comes from that most.) Tj
/Times 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 72 528 Tm
() Tj
/Times 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 72 510 Tm
(The sea does not read the table. The table reads the sea, once, and then repeats itself) Tj
/TimesIt 12 Tf
1 0 0 1 72 492 Tm
(politely for a year.) Tj
/Times 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 72 470 Tm
() Tj
/Times 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 72 452 Tm
(In March 2024 we counted fourteen open anemones in a pool that should have been asleep.) Tj
/Times 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 72 434 Tm
(The guidebook says they close in winter. The guidebook was written from another coast,) Tj
/Times 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 72 416 Tm
(by people who had not met these particular anemones.) Tj
/Times 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 72 398 Tm
() Tj
/Times 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 72 380 Tm
(This is the small, ordinary scandal of field notes: the living thing declines to match) Tj
/Times 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 72 362 Tm
(the description. A careful archive should record the disagreement, not correct it.) Tj
ET
