1 0 0 1 72 720 Tm
(Driftwood Notes) Tj
/Times 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 72 690 Tm
() Tj
/Times 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 72 672 Tm
(Driftwood is the shore's mail: everything the sea could not deliver, left at the tide) Tj
/Times 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 72 654 Tm
(line with no return address. A good beachcombing day is a day when the sea has been sorting.) Tj
/Times 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 72 636 Tm
() Tj
/Times 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 72 618 Tm
(The rule at the field station: photograph it, note where it was, leave it where it lies.) Tj
/Times 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 72 600 Tm
(Driftwood belongs to the next high tide, not to us. The archive keeps the photograph and) Tj
/Times 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 72 582 Tm
(the coordinates; the object keeps its journey.) Tj
/Times 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 72 564 Tm
() Tj
/Times 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 72 546 Tm
(This is, more or less, how the whole atlas works. We are not collecting the coast. We are) Tj
/Times 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 72 528 Tm
(keeping a careful record of having noticed it.) Tj
/Times 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 72 510 Tm
() Tj
